A||||8||RedGTFieroKCMO||Anyone tried to QUIET down the interior???||||1||
Z||000000||RedGTFieroKCMO||12-27-2001||10:13 PM||||Anyone know if that Dynamat material works??  I think this car is just way too loud and creaky. I have a GT and can barely hear the stereo from the loud exhaust, road, and wind noise. <P>This isn't including the bumps that jar the teeth outta your mouth.<P>All ideas welcome,<P>Sean<BR>KCMO<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||12-27-2001||10:44 PM||||My 88 coupe was pretty quiet. It didn't have a V6 behind it roaring away though. It was also low miles and mint so all the seals were like new. I could cruse at 90mph all day long if I wanted to. Took it up to 110+mph a few times and it was very quiet, seems like it was less noisey at those speeds then it was at lower ones.<P>My 84 on the other hand is terrable! I hear things making noises and wind from everywhere  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. The 4.10's don't help. At 80 im runing like 4000 rpm. My duke has a pretty noisey exhaust also.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMontreal||12-27-2001||10:49 PM||||Tell ya what... change your exhaust system .. that should fix your engine noise problem.. roll up your windows.. this should also block a lot of unwanted noise.. and change your shocks.. this should fix the ride... oh and.. slow down when going over speedbumps... that Fiero isn't an SUV! <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Mine is very quiet when it works...<P>Take it easy<P><P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontrealholidays.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroHarry||12-27-2001||11:01 PM||||I get alot of wind noise from the sun roof, but after its back in place it only whistles a little <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>12"sub and Alpine amp did the trick for me!<P>Good luck trying to quite her down though, more miles = lots of noise.<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||6
Z||000004||artherd||12-27-2001||11:22 PM||||"It's a sports car, it's SUPPOSED to be loud!"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>That said, yes, Dynamat really works.  Very well infact.<P>These cars do come fairly loud, but wind noise will only be an issue if you have bad seals.<P>Also, the stock exhaust is actually stunningly loud for a Production car.  With a new Catalyst, the stock muffler is almost as loud as the same Catalyst on a Flowmaster !!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||Joe Torma||12-28-2001||02:09 AM||||I used dynomat in my car, but I really haven't driven it.<P>Hehe...I quieted it down to make it loud.  3200+watts should do it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||gtsonly||12-28-2001||09:12 AM||||Talk about noise, try a t-top!!! There is more creakin' and crackin' driven down the road at normal speeds and my seals are new. But I love the Noise!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero001_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
